  <title>DELETE Command (FoxPro)</title>
  <keywords>
    <keyword>Commands</keyword>
    <keyword>DELETE command</keyword>
    <keyword>DELETE command<keyword>FoxPro</keyword></keyword>
    <keyword>Records</keyword>
  </keywords>
  <body>
    <header>
      <para styleclass="Heading1">DELETE Command &#160;(FoxPro)</para>
    </header>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><snippet src="__FoxProOnly" inline="false"/><snippet src="__CommandInclude" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Purpose</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">Marks records for deletion, using the rules of the FoxPro dialect. This is the FoxPro version of the <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_DELETE">DELETE</link> command.</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Syntax</para>
    <para styleclass="Code with box">DELETE [&lt;Scope&gt;] [FOR &lt;lCondition&gt;] [WHILE &lt;lCondition&gt;] [NOOPTIMIZE] [IN &lt;WorkArea&gt; | &lt;Alias&gt;]</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Arguments</para>
    <para styleclass="List"><snippet src="__Scope" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="List"><snippet src="__While" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="List"><snippet src="__For" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="List">NOOPTIMIZE<tab />Disables the optimization of the FOR clause. This clause is accepted for compatibility.</para>
    <para styleclass="List"><snippet src="__In" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Remarks</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">The clauses can be specified in any order. Without a scope, FOR or WHILE clause only the current record is deleted. With a FOR clause the default scope is ALL.</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">DELETE only marks the records for deletion. The records remain in the table until <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_PACK">PACK</link> is executed. Use <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_SET_DELETED">SET DELETED</link> to hide the deleted records and <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_RECALL">RECALL</link> to remove the deletion mark.</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">After the command has completed, the variable _TALLY contains the number of records that have been marked for deletion. Records that were already marked as deleted are not counted.</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Examples</para>
    <para styleclass="Code Example">USE Customers<br/>DELETE FOR Country = &quot;XX&quot;<br/>DELETE NEXT 5 IN Customers<br/>? _TALLY</para>
    <para styleclass="Body Text"><snippet src="__IncludeLibRT" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">See Also</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_DELETE">DELETE</link>, <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_DELETE_FROM">DELETE FROM</link>, <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_RECALL_FoxPro">RECALL (FoxPro)</link>, <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_PACK">PACK</link>, <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_SET_DELETED">SET DELETED</link>, <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="html\Overload_XSharp_RT_Functions_DbDelete.htm" domain="XSharpRef.chm">DbDelete()</link>, <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="html\M_XSharp_RT_Functions_DbEval.htm" domain="XSharpRef.chm">DbEval()</link></para>
